se transition.\n- **Enforcement reference**: how the CI lint rule guards the convention and how contributors run it locally.\n- **Open content question** (recorded, non-gating): whether the convention should recommend optional fields beyond name/namespace/kind (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category) — a PM/Observability-team decision; the guideline documents the required field set regardless, and optional fields would be additive follow-up scope.\n\nPublication scope:\n\n- Publish the convention as the contribution guideline for new controller development in the rhods-operator repository.\n- Publish the convention for external operator adoption and file tracking issues in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects, per the strategy's mitigation for external adoption delay.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the convention documentation, when published, then it specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, the cluster-scoped-resource rule, and the three-problem diagnosis, measured by the published guideline containing each element.\n- Given the migration guide, then before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity and before/after query examples for the DSCI key migration are included, measured by the guide containing both example sets reviewed against the implemented code changes.\n- Given the guideline references the implemented behavior, then the content is technically reviewed against the actual conversion work in both binaries, measured by a documented technical review sign-off with no unresolved accuracy findings.\n- Given the external publication, then the convention is published for external operator adoption and tracking issues are filed in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects, measured by links to the published convention and the filed issues.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-8 (P1)**: document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publish for external operator adoption.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":51983,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91dd77060b3a4ac5","agent_id":"af4fb60619de8129c","session_id":"852e52ce-bfa6-41ab-90de-21ff2eb47c3f","uuid":"7aae4ae1-d30c-4e8f-abc3-c6a80ce36f18","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:57:34.577Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
