{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4f195d857b6999f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Manager binary reconciliation error log standardization\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Manager binary reconciliation error log standardization\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic standardizes reconciliation error logging across the rhods-operator manager binary. It resolves all three diagnosed problems — message-embedded resource identity, non-standard DSCI structured key names, and the missing `resourceKind` field — across the five controller tiers of the manager binary: the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller, and 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup), plus the 15 action files across 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module).\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- **Call-site audit**: identify all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager binary (controllers, module handlers, and the 15 action files), using grep/static analysis; classify each call site as embedding resource identity in the message string, missing `resourceKind`, using non-standard DSCI key names, or already conformant. Track coverage in a checklist. The strategy's 75%-embedding figure is an estimate to be confirmed by this audit.\n38\t- **Embedded-identity conversion**: for every reconciliation error log call that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string, extract the identity fields and convert to structured key-value pairs — e.g. `log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile Foo in namespace bar\")` becomes `log.Error(err, \"reconciliation failed\", \"name\", foo.Name, \"namespace\", foo.Namespace, \"resourceKind\", \"Foo\")`.\n39\t- **DSCI key-name migration**: migrate the DSCInitialization controller from the non-standard key names `Request.Name` and `DSCInitialization` to the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`), per the confirmed call sites in `dscinitialization_controller.go`.\n40\t- **`resourceKind` additions**: add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all reconciliation error logs — P0 for service controllers, the module controller and its 8 module handlers, and action files (where the kind is not implied by the controller name), and P1 for the DSC and 8 component controllers (cross-controller queryability enhancement; same call sites as the conversion work, so delivered in the same pass).\n41\t- **Action files**: cover all 15 action files across the 4 tiers — 8 component (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), 3 module (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n42\t- **Cluster-scoped resources**: ensure cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) emit `name` and `resourceKind` and do not emit a spurious namespace value (namespace omitted or empty string).\n43\t- **Backwards-compatibility verification**: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error; deploy a test build to a dev cluster with the production log consumer stack configured, trigger reconciliation errors, and verify Loki/CloudWatch ingest the new format without configuration changes.\n44\t- **Alert-rule coordination**: collect an inventory of existing text-based log alert rules that rely on message-string patterns changing in this conversion, and hand identified rule updates to SRE/Support. SRE/Support response time is externally controlled and tracked as a risk, not an acceptance criterion.\n45\t- **Release-notes content**: document the DSCI key-name migration in release notes with before/after query examples, so the transition happens in a single release.\n46\t\n47\tField naming follows camelCase (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) per the SME-specified convention aligning with controller-runtime's structured log key conventions.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given the audit deliverable, then a checklist of every `log.Error()` call site in manager-binary reconciliation error paths exists with classification (embeds identity / missing `resourceKind` / non-standard DSCI keys / conformant), measured by the checklist covering 100% of call sites found by the agreed grep/static-analysis pass.\n52\t- Given any manager-binary reconciliation error log call that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string, when the code is updated, then the call uses structured key-value pairs instead, measured by CI lint rule or static analysis flagging zero remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text.\n53\t- Given the DSCI controller's reconciliation error logs, when the code is updated, then all structured field names use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), measured by unit test asserting DSCI error logs contain the standard field names and a codebase grep confirming no references to `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` field names remain.\n54\t- Given a service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) or the module controller (with any of its 8 module handlers) encounters a reconciliation error, when the error is logged, then the log entry includes `resourceKind` as a structured field, measured by unit tests parsing test logger output and asserting `resourceKind` presence with the correct value.\n55\t- Given an action file error log across any of the 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module), when the code is updated, then the log entry includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind`, measured by unit tests asserting all three fields are present with correct values across all 15 action files.\n56\t- Given the DSC controller and 8 component controllers, when a reconciliation error is logged, then the entry includes `resourceKind`, measured by unit tests parsing test logger output (P1 requirement delivered in the same pass over the same call sites).\n57\t- Given a cluster-scoped resource (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization) is reconciled and encounters an error, when the error is logged, then the entry includes `name` and `resourceKind` and `namespace` is omitted or empty, measured by unit test confirming no spurious namespace value.\n58\t- Given the log format change, when a test build runs on a dev cluster with the production log consumer stack, then structured fields appear in the output and Loki/CloudWatch ingest both old and new formats without configuration changes, measured by a documented before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error.\n59\t- Given the DSCI key migration replaces existing field names, then the migration is documented in release notes with before/after query examples and lands in a single release, measured by the release-notes content being reviewed and merged alongside the code change, and the SRE/Support alert-rule inventory with identified rule updates being delivered.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: conversion of message-embedded resource identity to structured KV pairs — manager binary portion.\n64\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: DSCI controller migration from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to camelCase key names.\n65\t- **HLR-3 (P0)**: `resourceKind` in service controller error logs.\n66\t- **HLR-4 (P0)**: `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` in all 15 action files across 4 tiers.\n67\t- **HLR-6 (P0)**: `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` in module controller error logs (8 module handlers).\n68\t- **HLR-7 (P1)**: `resourceKind` in DSC and component controller error logs — bundled with the P0 conversion work because it edits the same `log.Error` call sites in the same files; a split would double-touch the same files and duplicate the audit.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9905345d4062dd44","agent_id":"a7474fa0eec5b12ff","session_id":"852e52ce-bfa6-41ab-90de-21ff2eb47c3f","uuid":"e33da4f2-8602-4f9e-974b-482c9f77e6d0","timestamp":"2026-10-26T08:59:43.075Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4f195d857b6999f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
