{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c695302b00bd858","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: CI lint rule enforcing structured log fields\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# CI lint rule enforcing structured log fields\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the CI enforcement for the structured log field convention: a lint rule (or static analysis check) that flags `log.Error` calls in rhods-operator reconciliation paths which embed resource name or namespace in the message string or are missing the required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`). It is the durable regression-prevention mechanism named in the strategy's acceptance criteria and risk mitigations, and it applies to both the manager and cloudmanager binaries.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- **Lint rule implementation**: a CI-executable check (e.g., a golangci-lint custom rule or a static-analysis script) that detects:\n38\t  - `log.Error` calls in which resource name or namespace values are interpolated into the message string rather than passed as structured key-value pairs;\n39\t  - `log.Error` calls in reconciliation error paths missing required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`).\n40\t- **CI integration**: wire the check into the repository's CI pipeline so it runs on every pull request, covering manager and cloudmanager code.\n41\t- **Phased enforcement**: land the rule in warning/report-only mode initially, because the conversion of existing call sites proceeds in parallel; document the conditions for switching to enforcing mode (once the existing reconciliation error log calls are converted, the rule gates merges).\n42\t- **Local developer workflow**: document how to run the check locally so contributors can self-verify before opening a pull request.\n43\t- **Validation fixtures**: before/after code examples used to validate rule behavior — pre-conversion patterns must be flagged, post-conversion patterns must pass.\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- Given a pull request containing a `log.Error` call that embeds resource name or namespace in the message string, when CI runs, then the lint rule flags the call, measured by the rule flagging the pre-conversion validation fixtures in a CI run.\n48\t- Given a pull request containing a conformant `log.Error` call with `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` structured fields, when CI runs, then the lint rule passes it, measured by the rule passing the post-conversion validation fixtures in a CI run.\n49\t- Given the rule runs on the current codebase, then it produces a report of non-conforming call sites consistent with the audit classifications, measured by the rule's output reconciling with the audit checklist for both binaries.\n50\t- Given the enforcement plan, then the rule's warning-mode default and the documented conditions for enabling enforcement are recorded in the repository documentation, measured by the documentation being merged with the rule.\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- **HLR-1 (P0, verification mechanism)**: the CI lint rule is the stated measurement mechanism for HLR-1 (\"measured by CI lint rule or static analysis flagging any remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text\") and the risk-mitigation regression guard for the convention across both binaries.\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d438a826920d487","agent_id":"a398ef34c6b494e09","session_id":"852e52ce-bfa6-41ab-90de-21ff2eb47c3f","uuid":"ee7e8a05-85d1-4759-9917-5997af19d20b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T09:07:14.270Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c695302b00bd858","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010"}
